# Meta_Progression_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Run-based games with persistent unlocks (roguelite).

## 2. This document owns
- Permanent unlock trees: characters, starting kits, facilities, currencies-converters.
- Meta economy: what run outputs convert to meta currencies, at what rates, with what caps.
- New-player versus veteran meta targets and reset (prestige) policy.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- In-run upgrades — Run_Structure_Design.
- Character mechanical kits — Gameplay/Character docs.
- Achievement definitions — UI_UX (referenced only).

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Meta philosophy / 2. Unlock trees / 3. Meta economy & conversion / 4. Caps & pacing / 5. Prestige policy / 6. New/veteran targets / 7. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Meta vs Run: single-home rule per stat (run-wiped vs permanent declared once).
- Conversion rates live here; run output values live in Run_Structure.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every unlock has an acquisition source and an effect target.
- Conversion loops are acyclic or explicitly capped (no infinite meta inflation).
